OL,3,GNEWSACouncil refuses to rule out tax
OL,4,Arise above 5%
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt said it was the result of rising
OL,7,Fcosts, a reduction in government
OL,8,Ffunding and demand for care services.
OL,9,FCouncils are required to hold a local
OL,10,Freferndum or seek permission from the
OL,11,Fgovernment if they want to raise
OL,12,Fcouncil tax by more than 5%.
OL,14,FAnd Mike Cox, the council's cabinet
OL,15,Fmember for finance, said the authority
OL,16,Fwas focussing on finding savings within
OL,17,Fits services.
